          "segment_id": "seg-898212c14f0f9bf351894bdf",
          "segment_index": 13,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-898212c14f0f9bf351894bdf",
          "source_text_sha256": "8acd0b791eca2655546bfcbf87d7547900eca9ab9e33d19168c70c2774c4ef6f",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On September 13, 2015, at 8:30 PM, two people on a balcony were intrigued by the silent movement on an ascending trajectory in the sky of five bright, yellow-orange lights. Three of them formed a triangle. Only one testimony was collected. Based on the objective elements defined in the investigation report (attached document), namely:\n\n- The orange or yellow-orange color identical to that of lanterns.\n- The number corresponding to a classic group release of lanterns.\n- The simultaneous movement of the lanterns, carried by the wind and creating an illusion of psychological shape.\n- The movement in the direction of the dominant wind.\n- The behavior identical to that of objects subject to no or low wind: low speed.\n- The short observation duration (1 to 2 minutes) compatible with the lifespan of lanterns.\n- The date: a Sunday evening, compatible with those favorable to the organization of lantern releases on celebrations.\n- The disappearance caused by the extinction of lanterns reaching the end of their life.\n- The absence of noise.\n- The presence nearby of open-air installations conducive to lantern releases, located in the direction of observation.\n\nThe GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\" for a probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "0deca197e0f2a4899f27b3f3fb7ddc1e944dc4819bb0593fc43e6a4a45abd1c2"
        }
      ],
